# Keep Docker build contexts small and free of secrets.
#
# Without this file the frontend image build would copy node_modules (hundreds of MB) into the
# builder stage, and the backend image build would carry the local virtualenv and the development
# database. It is also a safety net: .env must never be part of an image layer.

# --- secrets / local configuration ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- python ---
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.sqlite3
**/htmlcov/
**/.coverage

# --- node / frontend ---
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vite/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- runtime artefacts ---
**/media/
**/staticfiles/
**/logs/
**/*.log

# --- vcs / editors / docs that images do not need ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
docs/
README.md
LICENSE
pip-install.log